RACE READ (worker's rapid-fire-Undo flag): Server side is not racy — the
SettingsManager hands each handler a private copy (documented in
saveAndRecalc/saveAndRecalcIfScenario) and delete/restore share no mutable
state, so writes serialize. The intermittent "Undo not registering" is
consistent with a client/probe-timing artifact: many overlapping htmx
requests against the single shared #whatif-results target with OOB toast
swaps can land out of order under scripted rapid-fire. There IS a minor
client-side double-submit window — the Undo <button> carries no
hx-sync/hx-disabled-elt, so a second fast click can POST /restore for an
already-restored id and render an error instead of a silent no-op — but that
is a UX-robustness gap, not data corruption, is out of scope for this
display-only-signal attempt, and matches the worker's own read. FINDING for
the backlog / a11y lane (which is testing it live), not a FAIL.
